--TEST--
A `password_file` is read at boot and its content is the value `Core\Config::get` answers, as a `?secret string`, for the secret's own key written in the call; a name the program computed throws `LogicError`, and `Core\Config::all` renders every secret directive `<secret>` — `rule:config/a-secret-is-a-file-whose-content-is-the-value`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:config/a-secret-is-a-file-whose-content-is-the-value` makes a secret a file whose content becomes the value, so the key the
// program reads is `password`, not the `password_file` it was written as. Both
// are in force: the `_file` sibling stays set so an audit can name the file.
// The value is a `?secret string`, so the case compares it rather than prints it.
?secret string $password = Core\Config::get("db.main.password");
echo "password matches=", $password == " s3cr3t" ? "yes" : "no", "\n";
echo "file=", Core\Config::get("db.main.password_file") ?? "null", "\n";

// The rest of the block is untouched by the pass — a secret is one key of it.
echo "driver=", Core\Config::get("db.main.driver") ?? "null", "\n";

// A secret directive's name built at run time would answer a plain `?string`,
// so `get` throws instead of reading it.
string $block = "db.main";
try {
    Core\Config::get($block . ".password");
    echo "computed=read\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "computed=LogicError\n";
}
echo "computed host=", Core\Config::get($block . ".driver") ?? "null", "\n";

// `get` and `all` are one key set, so the secret's own key is in `all` too.
// Its value is not: a page or a log line that prints every setting prints
// `<secret>` for a password, whether it came from a file or was written inline.
array<string> $settings = Core\Config::all();
echo "all=", $settings["db.main.password"], "\n";
echo "inline=", $settings["db.inline.password"], "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
# `rule:config/the-root-is-config-else-nvs-toml-else-the-shipped-defaults` step 2's `./nvs.toml`, the tree this run resolves.
[db.main]
driver = "postgres"
password_file = "secrets/db"

[db.inline]
driver = "postgres"
password = "hunter2"
--FILE secrets/db--
 s3cr3t
--EXPECT--
password matches=yes
file=secrets/db
driver=postgres
computed=LogicError
computed host=postgres
all=<secret>
inline=<secret>
